              text: '```xml\n<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>\n<report>\n  <metadata>\n    <title>Quarterly Business Report</title>\n    <period>\n      <quarter>Q4</quarter>\n      <year>2025</year>\n    </period>\n    <document_type>Business Report</document_type>\n  </metadata>\n\n  <section id="executive-summary">\n    <heading level="2">Executive Summary</heading>\n    <content>\n      <financial_performance>\n        <metric name="revenue">\n          <value currency="USD" unit="billion">4.2</value>\n          <change type="year-over-year" direction="increase" unit="percent">15</change>\n          <drivers>\n            <driver>cloud services</driver>\n            <driver>enterprise software</driver>\n          </drivers>\n        </metric>\n\n        <metric name="operating_margin">\n          <value unit="percent">28</value>\n          <change type="quarter-over-quarter" direction="increase" unit="percent">4</change>\n          <comparison>\n            <prior_period>Q3</prior_period>\n            <prior_value unit="percent">24</prior_value>\n          </comparison>\n        </metric>\n\n        <metric name="customer_acquisition_cost">\n          <change type="period" direction="decrease" unit="percent">12</change>\n          <attribution>improved marketing efficiency</attribution>\n        </metric>\n      </financial_performance>\n\n      <market_expansion>\n        <description>The company expanded into three new markets.</description>\n        <markets>\n          <market region="Asia">Southeast Asia</market>\n          <market region="Europe">Eastern Europe</market>\n          <market region="Americas">South America</market>\n        </markets>\n      </market_expansion>\n    </content>\n  </section>\n\n  <section id="key-metrics">\n    <heading level="2">Key Metrics</heading>\n    <content>\n      <operational_metrics>\n        <metric name="active_users">\n          <value unit="million">45</value>\n          <change type="period" direction="increase" unit="percent">22</change>\n        </metric>\n\n        <metric name="monthly_recurring_revenue">\n          <value currency="USD" unit="million">350</value>\n        </metric>\n\n        <metric name="net_promoter_score">\n          <value>71</value>\n          <change type="period" direction="increase">\n            <prior_value>62</prior_value>\n          </change>\n        </metric>\n      </operational_metrics>\n\n      <organizational_metrics>\n        <metric name="employee_headcount">\n          <value>8500</value>\n          <distribution>\n            <offices count="12" scope="global"/>\n          </distribution>\n        </metric>\n\n        <metric name="rd_investment">\n          <value currency="USD" unit="million">840</value>\n          <value_as_percent_of_revenue unit="percent">20</value_as_percent_of_revenue>\n        </metric>\n      </organizational_metrics>\n    </content>\n  </section>\n\n  <section id="outlook">\n    <heading level="2">Outlook</heading>\n    <content>\n      <forecast>\n        <period>\n          <quarter>Q1</quarter>\n          <year>2026</year>\n        </period>\n        <revenue_guidance>\n          <range currency="USD" unit="billion">\n            <low>4.4</low>\n            <high>4.6</high>\n          </range>\n        </revenue_guidance>\n      </forecast>\n\n      <initiatives>\n        <initiative id="1" category="product_launch">\n          Launching the AI-powered analytics platform\n        </initiative>\n        <initiative id="2" category="ecosystem_growth">\n          Expanding the partner ecosystem\n        </initiative>\n        <initiative id="3" category="compliance">\n          Achieving SOC 2 Type II certification for all cloud products\n        </initiative>\n      </initiatives>\n    </content>\n  </section>\n</report>\n```\n\n### Tagging Decisions\n\n| Choice | Rationale |\n|---|---|\n| `<metadata>` block | Separates document-level information from content |\n| `<metric>` with `name` attribute | Enables consistent querying of all metrics across sections |\n| `<change>` with `direction` and `type` | Distinguishes YoY vs QoQ comparisons and increase/decrease explicitly |\n| `<financial_performance>` vs `<operational_metrics>` | Groups metrics by domain for easier targeted parsing |\n| `<initiative>` with `category` attribute | Allows filtering initiatives by type (compliance, product, growth) |\n| Numeric values isolated from units | Keeps values machine-readable without requiring string parsing |',
